Global bytes of one call, COMPUTED from the sizes and not measured (compulsory traffic, every element once; re-reads across query tiles are not counted); t = BH x S tokens, d = head dimension: prologue fused (int8 or e4m3 K and V read once, fp32 scales) 2 t d + 8 t; prologue unfused (dequantisation kernel reads them, writes bf16; attention reads bf16) 10 t d + 8 t; PyTorch composition (int8 and fp32 scales read, bf16 written, flash reads bf16) 10 t d + 8 t; raw bf16 K and V 4 t d; epilogue (output O): fused 2 t d (written once), separate 6 t d (written, read, written). Per configuration in the columns *_global_bytes_computed of e16_summary_fusion.csv.
